DialectForge Protocol — Patent Notice

================================================================================
PATENT PENDING
================================================================================

The DialectForge protocol and all related methods, systems, and architectures
are the subject of one or more pending patent applications filed by
John Dean Martin.

The patent claims cover, but are not limited to, the following inventions:

1. THREE-TIER TRUST MODEL
   A system for classifying running software into Native, Adopted, and
   Quarantine tiers, where each tier receives different cryptographic
   seeds and access permissions, and where untrusted software is
   automatically isolated in ephemeral cryptographic sandboxes.

2. HIERARCHICAL SEED DERIVATION ARCHITECTURE
   A method of deriving per-process, per-page, and per-zone cryptographic
   seeds from a single root seed using labeled HKDF, creating a tree
   structure where revoking a parent seed cryptographically invalidates
   all descendant seeds.

3. DIALECT CYCLE ROTATION
   A method of periodically rotating all cryptographic parameters in an
   operating system at timed intervals with randomized jitter, causing
   all derived encryption keys, sector maps, and keystreams to change
   simultaneously.

4. XOR AGGREGATE CONSENSUS NEGOTIATION
   A method for multiple parties to establish a shared cryptographic
   key by each contributing a seed proposal that is XOR-aggregated
   into a consensus value, without any single party controlling the
   outcome.

5. QUARANTINE ZONE LIFECYCLE
   A system of ephemeral cryptographic sandboxes with time-to-live
   expiration, where zone destruction zeroes the seed and renders all
   data encrypted under that seed permanently unrecoverable.

6. USB AUTO-QUARANTINE TRUST BOUNDARY
   A method of automatically detecting and isolating USB storage devices
   by locking the boot device identity at kernel initialization and
   placing all subsequent USB storage in quarantine zones with
   automatic cryptographic wipe on device disconnect.

7. PER-PROCESS MEMORY PAGE ENCRYPTION
   A system for transparently encrypting each process's memory pages
   with unique keys derived from that process's seed, with automatic
   hardware backend detection and software fallback.

8. ALL RELATED METHODS
   All methods, systems, and apparatus relating to the DialectForge
   protocol, including but not limited to: anomaly-triggered emergency
   rotation, cross-dialect ptrace prevention, tier-aware IPC
   enforcement, package quarantine pipelines, and encrypted filesystem
   sector hopping.

